@startuml value-filtered-pruning
' Value-filtered querying over a MappedDictionary: the iterator carries a value
' predicate (e.g. "visible in the current lexical scope"). Whole subtrees whose
' aggregated value summary cannot satisfy the predicate are skipped, yielding
' the documented 10–100× reduction in work for scoped completion.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #E8EAF6
  BorderColor #283593
  FontColor #102027
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFE0B2
  DiamondBorderColor #EF6C00
  StartColor #2E7D32
  EndColor #C62828
  ArrowColor #37474F
}

title ValueFilteredQueryIterator — prune by value scope (10–100× fewer terms)

start
:advance automaton along a dictionary edge\n(lock-step DFS as usual);
if (subtree's value summary can satisfy the predicate?) then (no)
  #FFCDD2:prune the entire subtree;
  note right
    Skips every term beneath this node
    whose value fails the scope predicate.
  end note
  stop
else (yes)
  if (terminal <latex>\land</latex> accepting <latex>\land</latex> value matches predicate?) then (yes)
    #C8E6C9:yield (term, distance, &value);
  endif
  :recurse into the surviving subtree;
endif
stop
@enduml
